## 4. The Execution (Consequence or Release)



### Exists in Pine Labs docs


| Flow                     | Documented mechanism                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Fail — take the ₹500** | OTM **Presentation** API debits the blocked amount **to the merchant** (after subscription `ACTIVE`). No second UPI PIN.                                                                                                                           |
| **Fail — pay the peer**  | **Payouts API** `POST /payouts/v3/payments/banks` — pay beneficiary via `UPI` / `IMPS` / `NEFT` / `RTGS` (UPI uses VPA per docs). Money comes from the **merchant payout / funding account**, not as a direct bank-to-peer hop from the OTM block. |
| **Pass — don’t charge**  | Product intent: **release** the OTM block (see Trap gap — public release API incomplete).                                                                                                                                                          |




### Missing / gaps


| Gap                                | Detail                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Not one “route OTM → peer” API** | Documented unhappy path is **two steps**: Presentation (user → merchant) **then** Payout (merchant → peer). Not atomic; not “instant irreversible” in one call. Create Payout responses can be `SCHEDULED`. |
| **Merchant float**                 | Payout requires funded merchant payout capacity. If Presentation succeeds but Payout fails, money sits with merchant — your reconciliation needed.                                                          |
| **Pass release API**               | Still blocked on Pine Labs documenting/confirming release for OT-direct subscriptions.                                                                                                                      |
| **Social shame / survey claims**   | Product/messaging only; no vendor API.                                                                                                                                                                      |


